# Workflow scripts are read from disk and passed through a permission dialog that rejects control
# characters, so a CRLF checkout makes them unrunnable. Keep them LF on every platform.
*.js text eol=lf
# .mjs is the same rule and was missed until 2026-08-21, when the eval harness could not be
# launched: evals/harness/*.mjs had been pure CRLF since it was written, and the permission
# dialog rejected it as containing control characters. The comment above named that exact
# failure while its own pattern did not cover the file it was written to protect.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# The gate and its tools are executed by CI on Linux and locally on Windows; LF everywhere avoids
# a class of shebang and heredoc breakage that only shows up on one of the two.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Prose and data files were left unpinned until 2026-08-07, so on Windows every `git add` printed a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning for each one: dozens per bundle PR, enough that a real warning
# would have been lost in them. The gate and the CI steps read these files on Linux and locally on
# Windows, and the repo-wide dash sweep reads them byte by byte, so one ending everywhere is also one
# fewer difference between what CI sees and what an author sees.
*.md text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
